35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The technicians are gone, and our senior analysts are abroad. Yet the glasshouse crew remains strong. We must weigh this carefully.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The ledgers show frozen travel costs, but animal day rates spiked. Computing is free, though. This changes what the grant actually buys.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks! One engineer covers three institutes. That’s a huge risk for any project needing that equipment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that idle suite is a nightmare. But my data shows breeding colonies overrun twice as often. Computation is safer, and deposits now clear in weeks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The closeout files are damning. Catalogue awards still draw users a decade later. Mechanism-focused ones stalled. I trust the data, not the hype.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, your caution is wise. Yet the glasshouse crew stands ready. We must match the project to the hands we actually possess.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, that aligns with my findings. Simulation is now free, but animal care costs surged. We must match the science to the affordable, available resources.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that idle suite is terrifying. But the animal facility is accredited and has vets now. Glasshouses are packed, though. Who can actually run?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the accreditation is good, but the glasshouse is booked solid. That’s a bottleneck. I’d rather avoid the scheduling nightmare entirely.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the data confirms it. Live colonies overrun twice as often. I favor projects where the main risk is computation, not biology.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the glasshouse crew is whole, but the modelling minds are absent. We must choose a path where our remaining hands are sufficient.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I hear you. With modelling analysts gone, free computing hours are a lifeline. We must pick a project that doesn’t rely on those missing hands.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, that’s a tough spot. If the analysts are gone, can we even run the simulations? I’m worried about the bottleneck.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the repository migration is the key. Deposits clear in weeks now, not months. That administrative friction is gone, making data-heavy projects far more viable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the absence of analysts is a risk, but the data is clear. Computation-based projects deliver. I will not gamble on live colonies again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the absence of analysts is a risk, but the data is clear. Computation-based projects deliver. I will not gamble on live colonies again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, the free computing hours are a lifeline, but we still need people to run them. Let’s hope the remaining staff can manage the load.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that’s good news! But if the analysts are gone, who actually runs the simulations? I’m worried about the bottleneck.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the applicants for modelling posts are arriving in numbers. The bottleneck is temporary, not permanent.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, applicants are not yet staff. I stand by the closeout data: computation-based projects deliver reliably. I will not gamble on live colonies again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
